I'm looking for any published papers, books, or articles that discuss
how to consolidate large deployed Unix applications onto the same
server.

In an effort to cut costs, we are considering a transition of our
production environment from dedicated servers that run multiple
instances of a single application, to higher-powered servers that run
multiple instances of multiple applications.  In looking for
applications that are candidates for consolidation onto the same Unix
server, we are considering factors such as:  CPU utilization, I/O
traffic and network utilization, number of simultaneous users supported,
common shared libraries, reliability, etc.

Pehaps other companies and organizations have encountered this "server
consolidation" problem in the past, and I'm wondering if there are any
published papers or books that address the various issues involved, or
that suggest a process for conducting the consolidation.

Thanks for any pointers or help!

