Thomas,

This looks like it was a mistake that we tried to correct in DCE 1.1.
You are probably using an IBM DCE based on DCE 1.0.3.

I'm not sure if this will be much help, 
but in <dce/idlbase.h> in the 1.1 source if the following:

/*
 * when compiling DCE programs and/or libraries, we want the base type
 * of idl_char to be "unsigned char" (IDL doesn't support signed chars).
 * However, we compiling external programs, we want idl_char to have
 * the char type native to the platform on which the program is being
 * compiled. So ... use a macro that should only be defined if we
 * are building the RPC runtime of the IDL compiler.
 */

#ifndef IDL_CHAR_IS_CHAR
typedef unsigned char idl_char ;
#else
typedef char idl_char ;
#endif /* idl_char */

You may be able to retrofit you header file with this change.

I would certainly contact IBM and ask them to investigate
patching their DCE product with a similar fix if their compiler 
chokes in your (not uncommon?) situation.

-- 
